{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JsCeqBubDdaaXa7Ck6tRek","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/-\n2\t  Renewal transport change: design proof.\n3\t\n4\t  Models the PROPOSED change: the renewal credential moves from the request body into an\n5\t  HttpOnly cookie. Pure functions and Hoare-style statements; no traces or timing this pass.\n6\t\n7\t  `storedRenewalOk` is the server's stored renewal record for the session.\n8\t  The cookie's content is left opaque (`cookieValue`).\n9\t-/\n10\t\n11\tinductive Outcome | renewed | signedOut\n12\t  deriving DecidableEq, Repr\n13\t\n14\tstructure Session where\n15\t  storedRenewalOk : Bool\n16\t  cookieValue     : Nat   -- opaque\n17\t  cookiePresent   : Bool\n18\t\n19\tdef renewViaBody (s : Session) : Outcome :=\n20\t  if s.storedRenewalOk then .renewed else .signedOut\n21\t\n22\tdef renewViaCookie (s : Session) : Outcome :=\n23\t  if s.cookiePresent then (if s.storedRenewalOk then .renewed else .signedOut) else .signedOut\n24\t\n25\t/-- R-1: with the cookie present, the change is transport-only, not semantic. -/\n26\ttheorem transport_only (s : Session) (h : s.cookiePresent = true) :\n27\t    renewViaCookie s = renewViaBody s := by\n28\t  unfold renewViaCookie renewViaBody; simp [h]\n29\t\n30\t/-- R-2: a valid renewal never signs the user out. -/\n31\ttheorem valid_renewal_keeps_session (s : Session) (hc : s.cookiePresent = true)\n32\t    (hv : s.storedRenewalOk = true) : renewViaCookie s = .renewed := by\n33\t  simp [renewViaCookie, hc, hv]\n34\t\n35\t/-- R-3: a missing cookie signs out (no silent success). -/\n36\ttheorem no_cookie_signs_out (s : Session) (hc : s.cookiePresent = false) :\n37\t    renewViaCookie s = .signedOut := by\n38\t  simp [renewViaCookie, hc]\n39\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d764b45-a594-40cc-aa39-e43d050a2c21","uuid":"4ef7bbcb-d9a6-498f-8d96-39bbbcbe1f4c","timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:12:58.944Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/tmp.Anf4p4lr1b/proofs/Renewal.lean","content":"/-\n  Renewal transport change: design proof.\n\n  Models the PROPOSED change: the renewal credential moves from the request body into an\n  HttpOnly cookie. Pure functions and Hoare-style statements; no traces or timing this pass.\n\n  `storedRenewalOk` is the server's stored renewal record for the session.\n  The cookie's content is left opaque (`cookieValue`).\n-/\n\ninductive Outcome | renewed | signedOut\n  deriving DecidableEq, Repr\n\nstructure Session where\n  storedRenewalOk : Bool\n  cookieValue     : Nat   -- opaque\n  cookiePresent   : Bool\n\ndef renewViaBody (s : Session) : Outcome :=\n  if s.storedRenewalOk then .renewed else .signedOut\n\ndef renewViaCookie (s : Session) : Outcome :=\n  if s.cookiePresent then (if s.storedRenewalOk then .renewed else .signedOut) else .signedOut\n\n/-- R-1: with the cookie present, the change is transport-only, not semantic. -/\ntheorem transport_only (s : Session) (h : s.cookiePresent = true) :\n    renewViaCookie s = renewViaBody s := by\n  unfold renewViaCookie renewViaBody; simp [h]\n\n/-- R-2: a valid renewal never signs the user out. -/\ntheorem valid_renewal_keeps_session (s : Session) (hc : s.cookiePresent = true)\n    (hv : s.storedRenewalOk = true) : renewViaCookie s = .renewed := by\n  simp [renewViaCookie, hc, hv]\n\n/-- R-3: a missing cookie signs out (no silent success). -/\ntheorem no_cookie_signs_out (s : Session) (hc : s.cookiePresent = false) :\n    renewViaCookie s = .signedOut := by\n  simp [renewViaCookie, hc]\n","numLines":39,"startLine":1,"totalLines":39}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JsCeqBubDdaaXa7Ck6tRek","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
